invariant: INV-16
file: mlkem_poly.c
catches: test/lint-wide-multiply.sh
reason: KyberSlash's compression, the rounded quotient of a secret
  coefficient by the constant q. clang writes the quotient as a multiply
  by q's reciprocal on every spec, umull on the M3, multu on mips32r2 and
  mulhu on rv32imac, which the multiply count holds at zero. The Arm gcc
  at -Os writes udiv instead, and the m3 job's division count holds it
  (docs/decisions.md 156)

--- old
    uint64_t t = ct_widemul_opaque(((uint32_t)x << d) + 1664U, 1290168U);
    return (uint16_t)((t >> 32) & ((1U << d) - 1U));
--- new
    uint32_t scaled = ((uint32_t)x << d) + 1664U;
    return (uint16_t)((scaled - scaled % 3329U) / 3329U % (1U << d));
